{
  "description": "The reading of requirement headings (schema atlas-requirements version 4): RequirementHeadings.cs, RequirementTree.Read, the index (ProjectorIndex) and the web's readers answer each case's content with its rows. A top-level heading whose attrs.state is a string is a requirement; its section runs to the next heading. Fixed places: the dependency line is the node directly under the heading when it is a paragraph with attrs.dependencies true; a dependencies paragraph anywhere else is a note. Its pageReference atoms whose id is a page id (D form) and whose url has a valid ?heading= are the dependencies, the headingId for this page (pageId; without one, a requirement heading id of the document), pageId#headingId for another, each once. The party is the heading's attrs.party trimmed of spaces and no-break spaces, its contact attrs.partyContactId when the party is not empty. The facts line is the next node (after the dependency line, or directly under the heading) when it is a paragraph whose whole text, trimmed of spaces and no-break spaces, is 'do d. M. yyyy' (a space or a no-break space between the parts, a day in the calendar); its deadline as yyyy-MM-dd; else there is none and an od/pro line is a note. The text of a line (marks do not matter): text, a hard break as a space, a contactInline as its contacts[0].name, a youtrackIssue as its key trimmed of spaces, a pageReference as its title. A title: text, a hard break as a space, a youtrackIssue as its key, trimmed of spaces. Rows of requirement blocks (the old shape) are as before; positions count both in document order. A case with 'legacy' is also the move of a version-3 page (§6): its legacy content moved gives exactly its content. The version-3 facts line is at the same place, a paragraph whose first ' · ' segment (trimmed) starts with 'od ' or 'pro ' or is 'do d. M. yyyy'; its party is the rest of the first od/pro segment, its contact the objectId of a contactInline only when the party segment is exactly that chip (its name is the party), its deadline the first valid do segment. A line that is already a deadline line stays. Otherwise the heading gets party (and partyContactId when there is a contact) when the party is not empty and at most 200 characters (a longer one leaves the heading without a party and the line kept), and the line is replaced by the deadline line 'do d. M. yyyy' (none without a deadline), followed by the line itself unless the line is clean: only text and at most one contactInline, each segment an od/pro party or a valid deadline, at most one of each. Nothing else in the document changes.",
